// std/window/__native_win32.nori: the `nori_win_*` seam of window.nori on Windows, in Nori, for a
// program built with `noric --build --native --target x86_64-w64-mingw32`. It answers the calls
// window_win32.c answers in an LLVM build, over user32, gdi32 and shell32.
//
// The window lives on a thread of its own, which creates it and receives its messages: a Win32 message
// queue belongs to the thread that made the window, and the render loop above this seam runs on
// whichever scheduler worker resumes it. The window thread pushes what each message means into a queue
// any thread may read.
//
// Keys are reported as X11 keysyms and coordinates in logical pixels (physical ones scaled by 96/DPI),
// the seam's contract on every platform.
//
// A window record, in 8-byte fields:
//   0 hwnd  8 w  16 h  24 closed  32 px  40 py  48 btn  56 mid  64 lx  72 ly  80 tap_latch
//   88 qhead  96 qtail  104 queue (128 events of 4 x 8 bytes)  112 drop text  120 scroll remainder
//   128 locked  136 warp_x  144 warp_y  152 cursor shape  160 dpi  168 thread  176 ready event
//   184 wake event  192 queue lock  200 start w  208 start h  216 title (UTF-16)

